Story A: Cornelius was an astronomer, with stars and galaxies always on his mind, and was gradually working on turning his home into an observatory. In the midst of this remodeling, Agatha, the wife of Cornelius, griped about Cornelius focusing too much on the house renovation (which made the house unlivable) versus his job, which was astronomy. “Agatha is right”, Cornelius thought, and he went back to thinking about nothing but astronomy. However, when Cornelius was walking through his house one evening, his weight caused a floor still under construction to collapse. His resulting severe injury made Cornelius realize that he should try to do a better job at figuring out how much time to spend on astronomy versus fixing up his house.

Story B: Cornelius was an astronomer who thought about nothing but astronomy. He was obsessed with stars and galaxies. His wife Agatha complained that he was spending too much time on astronomy and not enough on maintaining his own house. As a result, the roof was gradually leaking more and more and the house was becoming almost unlivable. But Cornelius would not listen. Then, one evening when Cornelius was walking through his house, a rotten floor collapsed under his weight. Cornelius was severely injured but the accident showed him that Agatha had been right all along. He decided to try to balance his time between astronomy and maintaining his home.

